Q3, Q4, Q5: check every size a peer declares, and cap what is buffered

Every size in a Quick Share frame is the peer's claim. Upstream uses them
before checking them:

- Q3: a BYTES payload (the sharing frames that set a transfer up, and
  texts) is refused only when its declared total_size is over 5 MiB, so
  a negative size passes, and `Vec::with_capacity(total_size as usize)`
  turns it into a capacity near 2^64: it panics ("capacity overflow"),
  which ends the connection task (and the whole process in a build with
  panic = "abort"), before any consent, on both the receiving and the
  sending side.
- Q4: the buffer then grows by whatever the chunks carry, never checked
  against the declared size, and a finished buffer stays in the map for
  the life of the connection; any number of payload ids can be open at
  once. A peer can make the receiver hold unbounded memory before the
  user has seen anything.
- Q5: file sizes in the introduction are summed with `as u64`, so a
  negative size wraps the total the user is asked to accept, and nothing
  limits the number of files or keeps payload ids unique (two files
  with one id share one book-keeping entry and one output file).
- A file chunk is checked against the declared size with unchecked
  addition, and a last chunk that ends the file short is taken as the
  whole file: the transfer is reported finished with a truncated file.

The new hdl/payload.rs reassembles BYTES payloads for both handlers:
sizes below zero and over a cap (256 KiB for a sharing frame, 64 KiB for
a text) are refused, nothing is allocated from a declared size (only
from bytes that arrived), a payload never grows past what it declared,
every chunk must declare the same size, a finished or refused payload is
forgotten, and at most two are reassembled at once.

The introduction is refused (Status REJECT) when a file size is below
zero, more than 1000 files are offered, or a payload id repeats; a text
must declare 0 to 64 KiB and come alone. File chunks use checked
arithmetic, the last chunk may carry data, and it must end the file at
exactly its declared size.

Findings: Q3, Q4, Q5 (spec §5), S4, S6. Report: docs/UPSTREAM-QUICKSHARE.md Q3, Q4, Q5, R8.
